        "original_id": "4dcf1f43-df7f-5802-bdb7-004f37337f18",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rensselaer Plateau, Adirondack Mountains, eastern North America, eastern Quebec, Nova Scotia, New England, Appalachians, western North Carolina\n- Plants: Picea rubens, red spruce, Eastern White Pine, Eastern Hemlock, Balsam Fir, Red Pine, Tamarack\n\nFacts:\n- The Rensselaer Plateau has vegetation more similar to the Adirondack Mountains than to surrounding areas.\n- The Rensselaer Plateau has abundant Eastern White Pine, Eastern Hemlock, red spruce, and Balsam Fir.\n- The Rensselaer Plateau has more limited occurrences of Red Pine and Tamarack.\n- Picea rubens is commonly known as red spruce.\n- Picea rubens is a species of spruce native to eastern North America.\n- Picea rubens ranges from eastern Quebec to Nova Scotia and from New England south through the Adirondack Mountains and Appalachians to western North Carolina.",
